1
00:00:15,339 --> 00:00:17,422
HA JUNG-WOO

2
00:00:17,423 --> 00:00:19,423
IM SOO-JUNG

3
00:00:22,793 --> 00:00:25,023
KIM JUN-HAN

4
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:27,317
KRYSTAL JUNG

5
00:00:33,805 --> 00:00:35,602
SHIM EUN-KYUNG

6
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:59,104
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

7
00:00:59,105 --> 00:01:02,271
ONE MONTH AGO

8
00:01:21,671 --> 00:01:24,705
ORIGINAL GUL-DARI INSTANT TTEOKBOKKI

9
00:01:37,438 --> 00:01:39,905
Is there anyone here
picky about food?

10
00:01:40,953 --> 00:01:42,070
This place

11
00:01:42,071 --> 00:01:44,237
makes it so good,
no one will notice if someone drops.

12
00:01:44,238 --> 00:01:45,071
Hmm.

13
00:01:56,296 --> 00:01:57,995
I added plenty of liver and lungs.

14
00:01:57,996 --> 00:01:59,129
Thank you.

15
00:02:02,162 --> 00:02:03,462
Enjoy.

16
00:02:09,962 --> 00:02:11,212
Pig liver

17
00:02:11,762 --> 00:02:12,529
and lungs.

18
00:02:21,562 --> 00:02:23,029
You should eat as well.

19
00:02:23,762 --> 00:02:25,029
Do kids these days

20
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:27,463
not like sundae or tteokbokki?

21
00:02:31,662 --> 00:02:32,796
Oh, vegan?

22
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:34,795
Well,

23
00:02:34,796 --> 00:02:37,061
I tried that once,

24
00:02:37,062 --> 00:02:38,229
but it didn't go well.

25
00:02:39,696 --> 00:02:41,129
Right, madam?

26
00:02:41,662 --> 00:02:44,462
Oh, you need
to eat meat for strength.

27
00:02:50,896 --> 00:02:52,161
If they don't eat it, that's that.

28
00:02:52,162 --> 00:02:53,562
Why make such a fuss?

29
00:02:55,396 --> 00:02:56,262
Take it out.

30
00:03:00,929 --> 00:03:02,395
You all know about

31
00:03:02,396 --> 00:03:04,296
the ruins found at
the construction site, right?

32
00:03:04,929 --> 00:03:07,728
It's still under embargo,
so don't talk about it anywhere.

33
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:08,929
Take these.

34
00:03:09,429 --> 00:03:11,095
If you look inside,

35
00:03:11,096 --> 00:03:12,843
you'll see the changed zones marked.

36
00:03:14,962 --> 00:03:16,461
But within this zone,

37
00:03:16,462 --> 00:03:18,696
there are some buildings with squatters.

38
00:03:19,929 --> 00:03:22,039
If you secure those first,

39
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:24,061
I'll give you a chance
to join in on the shares.

40
00:03:24,062 --> 00:03:24,962
You know how much

41
00:03:26,229 --> 00:03:27,429
the dividends will be, right?

42
00:03:43,262 --> 00:03:44,495
Please eat.

43
00:03:44,496 --> 00:03:46,395
- Madam, it's been dipped in salt.
- Okay.

44
00:03:46,396 --> 00:03:47,296
Yes.

45
00:03:56,029 --> 00:03:58,796
Try to adjust
to the mood.

46
00:04:01,396 --> 00:04:02,496
You can do that, right?

47
00:04:08,596 --> 00:04:09,996
Just do a good job.

48
00:04:18,129 --> 00:04:24,462
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

49
00:04:26,396 --> 00:04:28,762
EPISODE 4

50
00:04:54,396 --> 00:04:55,261
What is it?

51
00:04:55,262 --> 00:04:56,029
Mr. Gi!

52
00:05:02,696 --> 00:05:03,762
He's a scary man.

53
00:05:10,729 --> 00:05:12,162
Let's make it official.

54
00:05:14,196 --> 00:05:14,929
Oh.

55
00:05:16,962 --> 00:05:18,129
That's a bit strange.

56
00:05:21,229 --> 00:05:23,295
They suddenly barged in,

57
00:05:23,296 --> 00:05:25,261
saying they had a deal with you.

58
00:05:25,262 --> 00:05:25,962
I see.

59
00:05:27,762 --> 00:05:28,596
Three billion.

60
00:05:29,536 --> 00:05:30,602
Sounds good, right?

61
00:05:31,096 --> 00:05:32,129
I raised it high.

62
00:05:42,668 --> 00:05:44,635
I'll give you some time

63
00:05:44,636 --> 00:05:45,509
to think about it.

64
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:47,582
Discuss it with your family too.

65
00:05:49,229 --> 00:05:51,560
This is your last chance
to do this quietly.

66
00:05:57,596 --> 00:05:58,762
Gyun? Gyun!

67
00:05:59,996 --> 00:06:00,929
Gyun!

68
00:06:05,562 --> 00:06:06,961
This coffee is good.

69
00:06:06,962 --> 00:06:07,729
Yes.

70
00:06:08,662 --> 00:06:09,829
NO ENTRY

71
00:06:13,662 --> 00:06:15,928
Can you close the toilet lid
when we do this?

72
00:06:15,929 --> 00:06:17,695
Why? Does it smell?

73
00:06:17,696 --> 00:06:19,934
But if we close the lid,
it gets slippery and won't work.

74
00:06:20,362 --> 00:06:21,396
Gosh.

75
00:06:33,896 --> 00:06:35,680
Are you sure this place is safe?

76
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:38,162
Oh, it's safe, of course.

77
00:06:47,996 --> 00:06:49,456
Come on, give it to me.

78
00:06:53,296 --> 00:06:54,777
Let's sell this building.

79
00:06:55,562 --> 00:06:56,828
Why suddenly?

80
00:06:56,829 --> 00:07:00,256
Sell this building to that Real Capital
or whatever they are.

81
00:07:01,896 --> 00:07:02,596
Jeez...

82
00:07:04,862 --> 00:07:06,229
What did I tell you?

83
00:07:09,996 --> 00:07:10,929
Let's go.

84
00:07:15,529 --> 00:07:17,059
So, we just sell it?

85
00:07:17,729 --> 00:07:18,596
Seriously?

86
00:07:19,629 --> 00:07:21,077
Don't you feel uneasy?

87
00:07:21,762 --> 00:07:23,834
Think about what you've done.

88
00:07:25,896 --> 00:07:27,922
Things may have gotten
a little tangled up,

89
00:07:28,229 --> 00:07:30,395
but I had
no bad intentions at all.

90
00:07:30,396 --> 00:07:32,228
I saw it in a movie where they called it

91
00:07:32,229 --> 00:07:34,796
redistribution of wealth
in situations like this.

92
00:07:35,242 --> 00:07:36,150
Kidnapping?

93
00:07:37,096 --> 00:07:38,462
Hey, somebody might hear you.

94
00:07:43,293 --> 00:07:44,434
I feel uneasy too.

95
00:07:44,896 --> 00:07:46,796
So let's sell the building and leave.

96
00:07:47,629 --> 00:07:49,102
Leave this place? And go where?

97
00:07:50,329 --> 00:07:51,096
To America.

98
00:07:51,362 --> 00:07:52,129
America?

99
00:07:52,829 --> 00:07:53,696
Yes.

100
00:07:54,496 --> 00:07:55,895
Let's go to America with Da-rae

101
00:07:55,896 --> 00:07:56,829
and start over fresh.

102
00:07:57,462 --> 00:07:59,462
Let's leave before it gets worse, okay?

103
00:08:02,596 --> 00:08:03,962
I don't want to live here any longer.

104
00:08:18,662 --> 00:08:20,717
Do you still smoke?

105
00:08:21,588 --> 00:08:23,354
Are you trying to meet the Lord early?

106
00:08:30,496 --> 00:08:33,196
If that's the Lord's will.

107
00:08:39,329 --> 00:08:40,995
Gosh.

108
00:08:40,996 --> 00:08:43,029
Nothing's changed here.

109
00:08:56,596 --> 00:08:58,129
Let's get to the point.

110
00:08:59,129 --> 00:09:00,301
Did you come because of the rumors?

111
00:09:00,729 --> 00:09:03,795
Well, I also wanted to see your face.

112
00:09:03,796 --> 00:09:04,962
I guess you knew.

113
00:09:05,596 --> 00:09:06,733
I may look like this,

114
00:09:07,596 --> 00:09:09,529
but I'm still pretty sharp.

115
00:09:10,062 --> 00:09:10,911
In that case,

116
00:09:11,496 --> 00:09:12,820
I'll get straight to it.

117
00:09:13,729 --> 00:09:16,129
I'll give you a good offer,
so hand over the building.

118
00:09:19,196 --> 00:09:20,729
Has it been about 20 years

119
00:09:21,896 --> 00:09:23,429
since our last conversation?

120
00:09:24,696 --> 00:09:25,562
Yes.

121
00:09:26,929 --> 00:09:28,494
It feels about that long.

122
00:09:28,841 --> 00:09:30,488
Time flies, doesn't it?

123
00:09:31,862 --> 00:09:33,896
Looks like you forgot
what kind of person I was.

124
00:09:34,796 --> 00:09:36,696
I remember very well.

125
00:09:37,996 --> 00:09:40,095
That bull-headed stubbornness.

126
00:09:40,096 --> 00:09:42,062
Not caring about anything.

127
00:09:42,929 --> 00:09:45,596
Thinks he's a strong person.

128
00:09:47,262 --> 00:09:49,591
Doesn't matter if others are struggling

129
00:09:50,096 --> 00:09:53,588
as long as you're doing well.

130
00:10:01,901 --> 00:10:03,301
How is Yi-gyeong doing?

131
00:10:04,596 --> 00:10:07,429
Do you have the right to ask that?

132
00:10:09,129 --> 00:10:10,391
And what about you?

133
00:10:11,309 --> 00:10:12,809
Do you have the right?

134
00:10:13,762 --> 00:10:15,172
I thought of Yi-gyeong

135
00:10:15,362 --> 00:10:17,239
like my own daughter.

136
00:10:17,829 --> 00:10:19,796
It was you who took her away.

137
00:10:20,462 --> 00:10:22,495
You were just making things worse.

138
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:23,584
And you're still like this.

139
00:10:25,662 --> 00:10:27,328
You need to be ready

140
00:10:27,329 --> 00:10:29,029
to grab the opportunity.

141
00:10:30,529 --> 00:10:32,229
You're just waiting around.

142
00:10:32,796 --> 00:10:33,729
So,

143
00:10:35,829 --> 00:10:37,561
are you happy?

144
00:10:37,562 --> 00:10:38,696
With your life?

145
00:10:38,895 --> 00:10:39,911
Oh.

146
00:10:40,896 --> 00:10:42,229
Enough bragging.

147
00:10:44,529 --> 00:10:48,029
Let's talk about your building plans.

148
00:10:48,462 --> 00:10:51,662
Have you thought about
what's the price of chasing money

149
00:10:52,729 --> 00:10:54,062
throughout your entire life?

150
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:57,515
Without money, what can you do?

151
00:10:57,516 --> 00:10:59,116
Better than to turn into a monster, right?

152
00:10:59,429 --> 00:11:01,461
Monster? Please.

153
00:11:01,462 --> 00:11:04,695
That's just a phrase
made up by jealous people

154
00:11:04,696 --> 00:11:06,762
who have money or skill.

155
00:11:07,147 --> 00:11:08,440
Just offer them money.

156
00:11:08,762 --> 00:11:11,062
They'll line up,
wanting to become a monster.

157
00:11:12,562 --> 00:11:13,542
Really?

158
00:11:14,196 --> 00:11:16,429
So you want Yi-gyeong
to end up like you?

159
00:11:21,696 --> 00:11:23,197
I won't sell the building.

160
00:11:26,136 --> 00:11:27,469
Especially not to you.

161
00:11:43,229 --> 00:11:44,775
Stop being stubborn

162
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:47,928
and think it over.

163
00:11:47,929 --> 00:11:48,896
REPRESENTATIVE JEON YANG-JA

164
00:12:31,996 --> 00:12:34,096
Gosh, why won't it open?

165
00:12:34,421 --> 00:12:36,137
Oh, that's loud.

166
00:12:36,429 --> 00:12:38,661
Mom, did you
change the password?

167
00:12:38,662 --> 00:12:41,374
Yes, it seemed like
the money's been leaking lately.

168
00:12:41,996 --> 00:12:44,162
Mr. Park told me to change the password.

169
00:12:44,468 --> 00:12:45,795
What's with Mr. Park?

170
00:12:45,796 --> 00:12:48,396
That person is a shaman.
Stop believing in superstitions.

171
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:54,562
You should've at least told me.

172
00:12:55,162 --> 00:12:56,728
Did you leave money with me?

173
00:12:56,729 --> 00:12:57,961
What's wrong?

174
00:12:57,962 --> 00:12:59,629
I always took it from here.

175
00:13:00,062 --> 00:13:01,328
I need money.

176
00:13:01,329 --> 00:13:02,761
I have to pay for
Hwal-sung's hospital bills too.

177
00:13:04,629 --> 00:13:06,549
You owe me three billion won.

178
00:13:07,629 --> 00:13:08,629
Three billion?

179
00:13:15,388 --> 00:13:16,305
Are you saying

180
00:13:16,862 --> 00:13:18,896
my worth is debt?

181
00:13:19,742 --> 00:13:21,409
That's still my money.

182
00:13:27,096 --> 00:13:28,162
Okay, I get it.

183
00:13:29,208 --> 00:13:31,108
Since it's your money,
let's consider it a debt.

184
00:13:32,129 --> 00:13:34,096
In that case, I'll borrow a little more.

185
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:35,495
What's the collateral?

186
00:13:35,496 --> 00:13:38,828
That apartment
in Jayang-dong that's under my name.

187
00:13:38,829 --> 00:13:39,895
I'll put that up.

188
00:13:39,896 --> 00:13:43,331
I transferred the title long ago.

189
00:13:43,562 --> 00:13:44,595
What?

190
00:13:44,596 --> 00:13:45,596
Whose name is it under?

191
00:13:47,529 --> 00:13:50,649
It was bought with my money.
Who do you think?

192
00:13:51,085 --> 00:13:54,028
You don't know what's
happening behind your back, do you?

193
00:13:54,029 --> 00:13:56,494
- You're so frustrating.
- Oh, Mom!

194
00:13:56,929 --> 00:13:59,895
Are you really my mom? How can this be?

195
00:13:59,896 --> 00:14:01,895
You're the only one
who stabs me in the back!

196
00:14:01,896 --> 00:14:03,392
No one else does that!

197
00:14:03,629 --> 00:14:05,728
Growing up under a mom
who's greedy for money

198
00:14:05,729 --> 00:14:08,196
and without a dad, do you have
any idea how hard it was?

199
00:14:08,796 --> 00:14:11,429
- I even gave up studying abroad...
- Enough.

200
00:14:12,545 --> 00:14:15,228
Among Hwal-sung's friends,
a guy named Su-jong,

201
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:16,929
isn't he the guy you met at the hospital?

202
00:14:17,596 --> 00:14:20,571
His building is in the redevelopment zone.

203
00:14:20,941 --> 00:14:22,375
Set up a meeting with him.

204
00:14:22,929 --> 00:14:23,862
What?

205
00:14:24,796 --> 00:14:26,462
I can't believe this.

206
00:14:26,762 --> 00:14:29,313
Su-jong's not selling the building anyway.

207
00:14:30,229 --> 00:14:32,129
Then we just need
to make him sell it.

208
00:14:41,929 --> 00:14:42,895
Is this enough?

209
00:15:02,596 --> 00:15:04,595
An iconic scene in artwork.

210
00:15:04,596 --> 00:15:07,428
Is it artistic allowance
made for dramatic effect

211
00:15:07,429 --> 00:15:11,195
or a scientifically possible fact?
Let's find out.

212
00:15:11,196 --> 00:15:12,562
Art Fact Check.

213
00:15:13,129 --> 00:15:16,261
Today, we're looking at

214
00:15:16,262 --> 00:15:20,161
the scene where Juliet comes back to life.

215
00:15:20,162 --> 00:15:21,695
Actually, Juliet

216
00:15:21,696 --> 00:15:24,395
didn't die from drinking poison.

217
00:15:24,396 --> 00:15:27,061
She took a sleep-inducing drug
that temporarily

218
00:15:27,062 --> 00:15:29,462
slowed her heartbeat and breathing.

219
00:15:29,996 --> 00:15:32,428
Hey, does that
really make sense?

220
00:15:32,429 --> 00:15:35,128
With anesthesia and
the right tools, it's not that hard.

221
00:15:35,129 --> 00:15:35,796
Really?

222
00:15:38,462 --> 00:15:42,128
When the heart rate
and temperature drop extremely low,

223
00:15:42,129 --> 00:15:44,529
it can look like someone is really dead.

224
00:15:48,862 --> 00:15:51,596
- I was watching.
- Huh?

225
00:15:53,262 --> 00:15:54,312
Da-rae,

226
00:15:54,996 --> 00:15:56,505
Mom and Dad

227
00:15:57,129 --> 00:15:58,296
have something to say.

228
00:16:03,096 --> 00:16:07,896
What is it? I have
an online interview study later.

229
00:16:08,596 --> 00:16:09,662
It'll be quick.

230
00:16:13,662 --> 00:16:14,562
Da-rae.

231
00:16:16,396 --> 00:16:18,228
Dad

232
00:16:18,229 --> 00:16:19,395
really

233
00:16:19,396 --> 00:16:20,762
loves you.

234
00:16:24,829 --> 00:16:27,962
Are you crazy?
Why are you saying this all of a sudden?

235
00:16:31,262 --> 00:16:34,028
Our whole family

236
00:16:34,029 --> 00:16:35,262
should go to America.

237
00:16:43,762 --> 00:16:46,595
Really? How?

238
00:16:46,596 --> 00:16:49,596
I was looking into dorms!

239
00:16:51,696 --> 00:16:52,961
You don't need

240
00:16:52,962 --> 00:16:53,996
a dormitory.

241
00:16:55,096 --> 00:16:56,962
Dad will buy a house

242
00:16:58,362 --> 00:16:59,428
with a pool.

243
00:16:59,429 --> 00:17:01,596
Don't overdo it.

244
00:17:04,229 --> 00:17:09,362
A house
with a lawnmower?

245
00:17:10,496 --> 00:17:11,961
Right.

246
00:17:11,962 --> 00:17:13,529
If you mow the lawn,

247
00:17:14,129 --> 00:17:16,696
I'll give you more allowance.

248
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:21,262
How much? Fifty dollars?

249
00:17:22,562 --> 00:17:23,828
Fifty dollars?

250
00:17:23,829 --> 00:17:26,096
Hmm, let's see.

251
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:31,129
If the exchange rate is 1,400 won,
that's too high.

252
00:17:32,929 --> 00:17:34,629
Forty-five dollars?

253
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:38,996
You two are funny.

254
00:17:40,475 --> 00:17:41,975
Get to the point.

255
00:17:44,362 --> 00:17:48,002
Our family should
all go to the U.S.

256
00:17:49,262 --> 00:17:50,361
and live there.

257
00:17:50,362 --> 00:17:52,695
Da-rae needs surgery too.

258
00:17:53,082 --> 00:17:56,821
I don't want our daughter to be alone.

259
00:17:58,162 --> 00:17:59,995
For our daughter's sake,

260
00:17:59,996 --> 00:18:01,128
that would be better.

261
00:18:01,129 --> 00:18:02,829
Both Dad and Mom

262
00:18:03,529 --> 00:18:04,796
want that.

263
00:18:18,829 --> 00:18:19,429
FAMILY

264
00:18:36,462 --> 00:18:37,596
REALTOR HEE-JU

265
00:18:39,374 --> 00:18:41,428
I'm sorry
for calling so late, Mr. Gi.

266
00:18:41,429 --> 00:18:44,661
But I really think I need to say this.

267
00:18:44,662 --> 00:18:48,139
Mr. Gi, please don't sell the building.

268
00:18:48,596 --> 00:18:50,428
You can't sell it right now.

269
00:18:50,429 --> 00:18:52,755
It's not easy to explain everything
in a text.

270
00:19:04,296 --> 00:19:06,062
Why? What's going on?

271
00:19:10,229 --> 00:19:12,029
Mr. Gi, are you still awake?

272
00:19:14,562 --> 00:19:15,841
I just woke up.

273
00:19:17,081 --> 00:19:19,581
I mean, what's the matter?

274
00:19:22,529 --> 00:19:23,196
Well...

275
00:19:34,529 --> 00:19:36,028
If you go over there,

276
00:19:36,029 --> 00:19:37,662
you can see the ruins excavation.

277
00:19:38,262 --> 00:19:40,695
That area isn't included
